# Windows batch files MUST have CRLF line endings. cmd.exe parses a bare-LF .bat
# one character out of step — every line loses its first character, `REM` stops
# being a comment, and the script fails with a screenful of
# "'X' is not recognized as an internal or external command".
#
# Both release.bat and start.bat were checked out with bare LF and were
# unrunnable by double-click, which is exactly how the README tells you to run
# them. Pin the ending so it cannot happen again.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts are the mirror image: they must keep LF, or bash fails with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M".
*.sh text eol=lf
